# Two independent original story drafts for each of the twelve themes.
# All language remains model authored and awaits independent review.
more=[
[("""A fishing village had to adapt when summer visitors began filling its narrow beach. Plastic cups appeared beside the boats, and the village council had to address the problem before the next holiday. The community opened a refill point so that visitors could reduce the number of bottles they used. Clean water was a shared resource, so the council published how much the service required. Volunteers used photographs as evidence of changing rubbish levels. They wanted to protect the shore without keeping visitors away. A sustainable plan also needed someone to clean the tap and check it every day. The first benefit was a tidier path. Whether the change would have a significant effect on the wider coast remained an open question.""","""游客增多后，渔村需要适应（adapt）海滩的变化，村委会着手处理（address）塑料杯问题。社区（community）设立补水点，减少（reduce）瓶子使用，并公开共享水资源（resource）的消耗。志愿者拍照取证（evidence），希望保护（protect）海岸而不拒绝游客。可持续的（sustainable）方案也需要日常清洁和检查。直接益处（benefit）是道路整洁，能否产生更显著的（significant）海岸影响仍待观察。"""),
("""At a school on a dry hillside, a leaking pipe became an unexpected lesson. The caretaker asked pupils to help address the problem by mapping every outdoor tap. They found a significant loss near the playing field. Rather than buy a larger tank, they discussed how to reduce waste and protect the limited water resource. The community paid for a repair and planted shade trees where the ground dried fastest. Pupils collected evidence by measuring the tank at the same time each morning. They learned that a sustainable system must adapt to the place where it is used. Its benefit was not simply a lower bill: the children could explain why the repair mattered and notice when another leak appeared.""","""干燥山坡上的学校漏水，管理员请学生通过绘制水龙头地图处理（address）问题。他们发现明显的（significant）损失，讨论减少（reduce）浪费、保护（protect）有限水资源（resource）。社区（community）资助维修并种树，学生每天固定时间测量水箱，收集证据（evidence）。他们理解可持续的（sustainable）系统必须适应（adapt）场地。益处（benefit）不仅是节省水费，也包括学生能解释维修意义、发现新漏点。""")],
[("""The village clinic tested a portable device that could monitor the temperature of its medicine cupboard. The team needed reliable readings during power cuts, not a long list of extra features. A nurse compared the data with a separate thermometer to check that it was accurate. Access to the results was limited to the staff who looked after the cupboard. No patient information was involved, but the clinic still explained its privacy rules. One innovation was a simple warning light that worked without an internet connection. The system made checking more efficient, yet it did not replace the nurse's judgement. When a door was left open, the light helped her discover the problem before the room became too warm.""","""村诊所测试可监测（monitor）药柜温度的便携设备（device）。团队需要断电时仍可靠的（reliable）读数。护士用独立温度计对照数据（data），检查准确性（accurate），只有负责人员拥有结果使用权（access）。虽然不涉及患者信息，诊所仍解释隐私（privacy）规则。无需联网的警示灯是一项创新（innovation），让检查更高效（efficient），但没有替代（replace）护士判断。"""),
("""A museum wanted to replace paper tickets with a small electronic device at the entrance. Before buying it, staff asked whether the change would make entry more efficient for every visitor. A reliable paper option remained available. The team chose to monitor waiting time rather than collect names. Accurate data would show where the queue slowed down without turning a visit into a record of personal movements. Privacy notices explained what was kept and for how long. Access to the machine was easy for wheelchair users, and staff could help anyone who found the screen confusing. The useful innovation was the combination of clear choices and human help, not the screen by itself.""","""博物馆希望用电子设备（device）替换（replace）纸票，先询问能否让所有访客更高效（efficient）入场，同时保留可靠的（reliable）纸票选择。团队监测（monitor）等待时间而不收集姓名，以准确的（accurate）数据（data）识别堵点。隐私（privacy）说明解释保存内容和期限，设备便于使用（access），工作人员也提供帮助。这项创新（innovation）由选择和服务共同组成。""")],
[("""A bicycle workshop offered a free evening class to adults who had never repaired a puncture. Its approach was to begin with a real wheel and one small question. The instructor tried to encourage each learner to explain what they noticed before touching a tool. Everyone could participate, but the individual pace was different. To assess progress, the instructor asked learners to show a partner how to check the tyre. Feedback focused on the next safe action. This method helped people develop practical knowledge without pretending that one lesson made them expert mechanics. The goal was to achieve a manageable repair and recognise when a damaged wheel needed professional attention.""","""自行车工坊的夜课以实物和小问题为教学方法（approach），鼓励（encourage）学员先描述观察。每人都能参与（participate），个人（individual）进度不同。教师通过请学员互相示范来评估（assess）理解，反馈（feedback）指向安全的下一步。这一方法（method）培养（develop）实用知识（knowledge），目标是完成（achieve）可掌控的修理，并辨认何时需要专业帮助。"""),
("""The language club wanted to develop a better way of practising new words. Its old method rewarded people who answered fastest, so quieter members rarely had time to participate. A student proposed a different approach: everyone would read a short notice and prepare one question. The leader used the questions to assess what the group understood. Individual mistakes became useful clues rather than public failures. Feedback included an example in another setting. The club still needed knowledge of grammar and vocabulary, but now it could encourage careful thinking as well as speed. Members hoped to achieve something modest: to understand a notice they might actually meet outside the classroom.""","""语言社团想发展（develop）更好的练词方法（method）。旧方式奖励抢答，安静成员缺少参与（participate）机会。新方法（approach）让每人读通知并提问，负责人由此评估（assess）理解。个人（individual）错误成为线索，反馈（feedback）提供另一情境的例子。社团仍需要语法词汇知识（knowledge），同时鼓励（encourage）思考，希望实现（achieve）一个实际目标：理解课外会遇到的通知。""")],
[("""The campus sports facility had a quiet room that few students knew was available. A volunteer proposed using it for a weekly clothing repair session. The first responsibility was to check that needles and other tools could be stored safely. A simple schedule made room for both the new group and existing users. Students offered to organise the sessions and support beginners. Staff helped maintain the equipment, but did not take over every decision. Finding a balance between independence and supervision took several meetings. The room became an opportunity to practise a useful skill and meet someone outside one's own course, rather than another space that could only be booked by an established club.""","""校园运动设施（facility）有一间可用的（available）安静房，志愿者（volunteer）提议每周修衣。首要责任（responsibility）是安全存放针具，日程（schedule）兼顾已有使用者。学生组织（organise）活动并支持（support）初学者，员工维护（maintain）设备而不包办。在独立和监督间取得平衡（balance）需要讨论，房间最终成为跨专业交流与练习的机会（opportunity）。"""),
("""Before examination week, a volunteer noticed students waiting outside a locked study facility. The room was available in the evenings, but nobody could find the correct schedule. She offered to organise a printed notice and asked staff who had responsibility for the key. A small team agreed to maintain the notice and support anyone making a first booking. They avoided a complicated new system that would itself need training. The aim was a balance between quiet individual work and group discussion. An opportunity had been hidden by unclear information, not by a lack of rooms. Making the rules visible was less impressive than opening a new building, but students could use the result immediately.""","""考试周前，志愿者（volunteer）发现自习设施（facility）外有人等待。房间晚间可用（available），却找不到日程（schedule）。她组织（organise）纸质通知，确认钥匙责任人（responsibility）。小组维护（maintain）通知，支持（support）首次预约者，平衡（balance）安静学习与小组讨论。机会（opportunity）被不清楚的信息掩盖，公开规则立刻改善了使用。""")],
[("""When a neighbour struggled to read a letter about a road closure, Tomas offered to help. Soon, several people began to share an hour each week at the local hall. They did not provide legal advice. They helped residents find dates, contact details, and the right office to call. The common aim was to improve access to information. The organisers wanted to include people who spoke different languages and involve them in choosing the session times. Trust grew because volunteers admitted what they did not know. A separate table offered help to repair small household objects. Visitors could ask a question without proving that they already belong to a particular group.""","""邻居（neighbour）难以理解封路信件，托马斯开始帮忙。大家在当地的（local）大厅共用（share）每周一小时，帮助居民找日期和联系人。共同（common）目标是改善（improve）信息获取，并纳入（include）不同语言人群，使其参与（involve）活动安排。志愿者承认知识边界，逐渐建立信任（trust）。另一张桌子提供小物修理（repair）；访客无需先证明自己属于（belong）某个团体。"""),
("""A row of flats had a common courtyard, yet most residents passed through it without speaking. One neighbour asked whether a monthly breakfast might improve things. People could share food, but bringing something was not a condition of entry. To include residents with different routines, the organisers changed the time from month to month. They tried to involve a local café without making the event a sales activity. Trust developed slowly through repeated, ordinary meetings. Someone offered to repair a bench, and another person brought a kettle. The courtyard did not suddenly solve loneliness. It gave people a place where they could begin to feel they belong, one conversation at a time.""","""公寓有共同的（common）庭院，却很少交流。邻居（neighbour）提议月度早餐改善（improve）情况。大家分享（share）食物，没带东西也欢迎。时间轮换以纳入（include）不同作息者，当地的（local）咖啡馆也参与（involve），但不做促销。信任（trust）在重复见面中成长，有人修理（repair）长椅。庭院没有突然解决孤独，却提供了慢慢产生归属感（belong）的机会。""")],
[("""A market stall sold vegetables that larger shops had rejected for their shape. Each consumer could purchase a mixed bag at an affordable price. The owner explained that the value lay in useful food, not a perfect appearance. Demand changed with the weather, so a steady supply was difficult to arrange. Buying too much would create more waste instead of less. The cost of collecting small deliveries also mattered. In the first season, profit paid for a modest investment in better storage boxes. The stall's future depended on careful estimates and returning customers. A good intention could open the business, but it could not replace the daily work of balancing what arrived with what people wanted.""","""摊位出售因外形被大店拒收的蔬菜，让消费者（consumer）以负担得起的（affordable）价格购买（purchase）。价值（value）在食用而非完美外观。需求（demand）随天气变，稳定供应（supply）难，多进货会增加废弃物（waste），零散运输也有成本（cost）。首季利润（profit）投入（investment）更好的储物箱，经营仍需精细估算。"""),
("""The owner of a small bookshop offered a repair service for worn books. A consumer could choose to keep a familiar copy rather than purchase a new one. The service was not always the cheapest option, so the owner showed the cost before starting. Some customers found it affordable because the book had personal value. Demand grew after a school asked for a group booking. A reliable supply of paper and glue became important, and an investment in training helped two assistants learn the craft. The shop recorded the profit from the service separately from book sales. Less paper waste was a welcome result, but each repair still required time and skill.""","""小书店修补旧书，消费者（consumer）可保留熟悉的书而非重新购买（purchase）。店主事先说明成本（cost），一些顾客因书的个人价值（value）认为价格可负担（affordable）。学校预约后需求（demand）增长，纸胶供应（supply）和培训投入（investment）变重要。服务利润（profit）单独记录，纸张废弃物（waste）减少，但修补仍需时间和手艺。""")],
[("""A colleague returning from leave found that important decisions were scattered across several message threads. The team agreed to review how it worked. For each task, a short shared note would state the owner, the deadline, and the next unresolved question. A flexible arrangement still needed a clear priority when several requests arrived together. People could collaborate across different working hours if they knew where to look. The solution was not to communicate more often, but to make necessary information easier to find. The manager measured productivity cautiously, checking missed details as well as completed work. A quieter chat window did not by itself prove success; fewer lost decisions were better evidence.""","""休假归来的同事（colleague）发现决策散落各处，团队重新评估（review）流程。每项任务（task）记录负责人、截止时间（deadline）和待决问题。灵活的（flexible）安排也需要明确优先事项（priority），才能跨时段合作（collaborate）。解决办法（solution）是让必要信息易找，而不是增加沟通（communicate）次数。经理谨慎评估生产效率（productivity），同时检查遗漏。"""),
("""A repair company wanted to review its habit of assigning every urgent task to the same experienced colleague. That system met one deadline while quietly delaying other work. The manager asked the whole team to collaborate on a flexible rota. A shared board showed the current priority and the skills needed for each job. Trainees could communicate when they needed help before a delay became serious. The solution included protected time for teaching, even though this reduced the number of jobs finished in the first week. Later, the team could handle absences more easily. They judged productivity over a longer period instead of expecting training to produce an immediate gain every afternoon.""","""维修公司重新评估（review）总让同一位资深同事（colleague）处理紧急任务（task）的惯例：一个截止时间（deadline）达成，其他工作却延误。团队合作（collaborate）制定灵活的（flexible）轮值，明确优先事项（priority）与所需技能。学员及时沟通（communicate）困难，解决办法（solution）包括留出教学时间。生产效率（productivity）用更长时期衡量。""")],
[("""The choir director noticed that rehearsals left some members tired and tense. She changed the routine to include regular pauses and a few minutes of gentle movement. The aim was moderate activity, not a fitness competition. Members discussed both physical comfort and mental concentration. A habit of ignoring discomfort had made it difficult to ask for a break. Now, people could stay active in a way that suited them and take time to recover when necessary. The director hoped to prevent avoidable strain, while recognising that personal health needs differ. Singing remained the shared purpose. Less stress came partly from knowing that a pause would be respected, not from a promise that one exercise could solve every problem.""","""合唱团把规律的（regular）休息和温和活动加入日常安排（routine），强调适度（moderate），而非竞赛。成员讨论身体（physical）舒适与心理（mental）专注，改变忽视不适的习惯（habit），按需要保持活动（active）和恢复（recover）。团长希望防止（prevent）可避免的劳损，也承认健康需求不同。压力（stress）缓解部分来自休息受到尊重。"""),
("""During a busy month at the bakery, the staff reviewed their early-morning routine. They agreed on regular short breaks instead of waiting until everyone felt exhausted. Carrying trays was physical work, but planning orders also required mental attention. The owner wanted to prevent mistakes caused by tiredness without asking people to work faster during the remaining time. A moderate change to delivery times gave the team room to recover between the busiest periods. They stayed active, but no longer treated constant hurry as a good habit. The staff did not claim that a timetable could remove all stress. They could say which parts of the day had become more manageable, and which still needed work.""","""面包店调整清晨安排（routine），加入规律（regular）短休息。搬烤盘是身体（physical）劳动，排订单也需要心理（mental）注意。店主希望防止（prevent）疲劳错误，适度（moderate）调整送货时段，让员工在忙碌间恢复（recover），保持活动（active），不再把匆忙当好习惯（habit）。日程无法消除所有压力（stress），但能具体说明改善之处。""")],
[("""The mountain village was not the destination on Daniel's original ticket. A road closure interrupted his journey, and the driver suggested an alternative route. Public transport would take longer, but it passed a village where accommodation was still available. During the delay, Daniel learned how weather shaped the local timetable. He chose to explore a short marked path rather than walk into unfamiliar hills alone. A shopkeeper explained which places visitors should respect by leaving them quiet. The experience changed his idea of a successful trip. Reaching every planned stop mattered less than understanding the choices made along the way. He kept the unused ticket in his notebook, beside the route he had actually travelled.""","""丹尼尔的目的地（destination）并非山村，但封路打断旅程（journey），司机建议替代（alternative）路线（route）。公共交通（transport）更慢，却经过仍有住宿（accommodation）的村庄。延误（delay）中，他理解天气如何影响时刻表，选择探访（explore）标记小径，并尊重（respect）需保持安静的地方。这段经历（experience）改变了他对成功旅行的理解。"""),
("""A family planned a journey by rail so their children could see how the landscape changed. Their destination was a lakeside town, and the route included a small station without a ticket office. They checked the transport information before leaving and chose accommodation within walking distance of the platform. When a delay removed their afternoon connection, the station notice offered an alternative bus. The children wanted to explore the town while they waited. Their parents explained how to respect private gardens and narrow paths. The experience included frustration as well as discovery. At home, the children drew a map of the journey, including the unexpected bus, rather than only the place where they had finally arrived.""","""一家人乘火车旅行（journey），目的地（destination）是湖畔小镇，路线（route）含无人售票站。他们预查交通（transport）并订车站附近的住宿（accommodation）。延误（delay）错过换乘，通知提供替代（alternative）公交。等待时孩子探访（explore）小镇，家长讲解尊重（respect）私人花园和小路。这次经历（experience）既有挫折也有发现。""")],
[("""A young designer created an original poster for the town's annual music festival. To understand its heritage, she asked older musicians to record how earlier festivals had been organised. Their accounts showed that tradition included change: instruments, venues, and audiences had never stayed completely fixed. A small exhibition placed contemporary photographs beside old programmes. Visitors could interpret the history in several ways rather than accept one official memory. The audience helped identify people whose names had been lost. The organiser wanted to preserve these contributions as part of the town's identity. The poster could attract attention for a week, but the conversations behind it created something that could remain useful after the last performance.""","""年轻设计师为音乐节创作原创（original）海报，了解遗产（heritage）时请老乐手记录（record）往届经历。他们说明传统（tradition）包含变化。小展览（exhibition）将当代（contemporary）照片与旧节目单并置，观众（audience）可多角度解读（interpret），并帮助辨认失名者。组织者保存（preserve）这些贡献，让其成为小镇认同（identity）的一部分。"""),
("""The village theatre invited residents to record stories about a bridge that was about to be repaired. An original play grew from the interviews, but the director made clear which parts were invented. The audience could also visit an exhibition of photographs and written memories. The project aimed to preserve local heritage without pretending that everyone remembered the same past. Contemporary concerns appeared beside older stories: school journeys, market days, and the fear of losing a familiar view. To interpret the bridge only as stone would miss its role in the village's identity. Tradition lived in the ways people used the crossing, not simply in a date carved above the water.""","""村剧场邀请居民记录（record）将维修的桥梁故事，形成原创（original）剧本，并说明虚构部分。观众（audience）也可观看照片和记忆展览（exhibition）。项目保存（preserve）地方遗产（heritage），承认记忆有差异。当代（contemporary）关切与旧故事并置。解读（interpret）桥不能只看石头；传统（tradition）和地方认同（identity）也存在于过桥方式中。""")],
[("""A resident asked why the public square felt difficult to cross despite having so much open space. The urban team watched how a pedestrian moved between the bus stop and the clinic. Traffic entered a side road just where the walking route narrowed. The design looked generous on a plan, but benches and signs interrupted the useful path. Better infrastructure began with moving those objects and making the crossing accessible. A new path would connect the library entrance to the bus shelter. The team tested it with people carrying bags, pushing prams, and using mobility aids. They learned that empty space and usable space were not the same thing, especially when someone needed to move slowly.""","""居民（resident）询问公共（public）广场为何难穿过。城市（urban）团队观察行人（pedestrian）从站台到诊所的路径，发现车流（traffic）与窄处冲突。设计（design）图面宽敞，座椅标牌却阻路。改善基础设施（infrastructure）先从移动物件、提升无障碍性（accessible）开始，新路连接（connect）图书馆与候车亭。空的空间（space）不一定好用。"""),
("""The city planned to connect two schools with a safer walking route. An urban survey first asked each resident where traffic made crossing difficult. One pedestrian described a corner where parked vans blocked the view. The public discussion moved from an attractive design drawing to the details of an ordinary school morning. Infrastructure included lighting, drainage, and enough space for children and adults to wait together. The route also had to be accessible to people who could not use steps. A temporary arrangement let the council test deliveries before building began. The final plan was less dramatic than the first picture, but people could explain how each change answered something they had actually observed.""","""城市准备连接（connect）两所学校，城市（urban）调查请居民（resident）指出车流（traffic）导致的困难。一位行人（pedestrian）提到货车挡视线。公共（public）讨论从漂亮设计（design）转向真实早晨：基础设施（infrastructure）包括照明、排水和等候空间（space），路线还需无障碍（accessible）。临时方案先测试送货，让改动回应实际观察。""")],
[("""Elena wanted to choose a useful birthday gift for her brother, who had recently moved into a small flat. At first she looked for another appliance. Then she began to notice how little room he had. A practical gift might save space rather than fill it. She chose a simple set of repair tools instead and asked a patient friend to explain their safe use. The quality of the instructions mattered as much as the tools. Her brother used them to fix a loose drawer and began to discover which small jobs he could manage. His confidence grew from understanding one task, not from being told that he should be able to repair everything alone.""","""埃琳娜想选择（choose）生日礼物，注意到（notice）弟弟公寓很小。实用的（practical）礼物应节省（save）空间，所以她转而（instead）买简单的（simple）工具，请耐心的（patient）朋友讲安全使用。说明质量（quality）与工具同样重要。弟弟修好抽屉，发现（discover）能处理哪些小任务，信心（confidence）来自真正理解一件事。"""),
("""On Saturday, Ben planned to choose new shelves for a crowded cupboard. A friend suggested checking what was already inside instead. They began to notice duplicate items and boxes that had not been opened for years. A simple list helped them discover what they actually used. Better quality storage would not solve the problem if the cupboard kept filling. The practical change was to leave a little empty space and save the purchase for later. Ben had to be patient with the process, especially when an old object brought back memories. Finishing one shelf gave him confidence to continue. The room became easier to use before a single new shelf had been ordered.""","""本想选择（choose）新架子的本，转而（instead）检查柜内物品，注意到（notice）重复和多年未开箱子。简单的（simple）清单帮助发现（discover）实际用途。更高质量（quality）收纳不能解决不断塞满的问题，实用的（practical）改变是留空，节省（save）购买。他耐心地（patient）整理，完成一层后获得信心（confidence）。""")]
]
